WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.580
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.180
What could it mean?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.900
Good morning!

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.790
Oh, it’s you guys.
Good timing.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.540
Satoshi and Go,
have you heard?

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.720
There’s something strange
going on in the Johto Region.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.540
Huh? What is it?

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:04.540
The sky in one town suddenly went pitch-black,
and they haven’t seen the sun rise since.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.460
The sky went pitch-black?

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.300
When do they eat breakfast
if it’s always night?!

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.180
<i>That’s</i> your question?

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.840
Satoshi has a point, though.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.140
This has to mess with
their daily rhythms.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.310
It must be hard
for the people there.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:22.730
We don’t know what caused it,
but Pokémon may be suffering, too.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.790
We’ll check it out!

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:27.780
I wanna know what
a never-ending night is like!

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:31.240
Of course. Would you go
and investigate, then?

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:33.680
All right! Off to Johto!

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.740
Let’s go!

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.220
A small town in the Johto region.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:23.350
It’s currently morning, and yet
the dark of night covers the town.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.870
It really is pitch-black...

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.980
But it’s not night right now...

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.860
It’s morning, right?

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:34.370
Good morning!

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:35.990
Looks like another
dark day today.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.610
The washing never dries.
It’s such a pain...

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.990
It’s kinda weird.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:41.870
Yeah...

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.400
Easy does it...

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.850
Good morning!

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:51.880
Oh, morning...

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:57.010
Not even exercising can cheer me up
when it’s this dark...

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.280
Is it always night here?

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:07.340
Yeah.
Been about a week by now.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.730
That long?

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:12.620
Without knowing the time,
I can never tell when to eat...

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.280
Look. Do you see that?

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.740
With the sun gone,
even the flowers are wilting...

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:25.160
The Yamikarasu are sulking.
Everyone thinks they’re bad luck.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:27.780
Bad luck?

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.930
Yamikarasu! Darkness Pokémon!
Evil/Flying type!

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:36.130
It is believed to bring misfortune
to all those who see it at night,

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.170
so it is feared and
loathed by many!

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.720
You don’t look too happy.
Wanna come with me?

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:45.100
Monster Ball, go!

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:56.730
Yamikarasu’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.390
I’m feeling sleepy...

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.690
Let’s go home, Usokki.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.710
Bye, mister.

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:08.330
Be careful in the dark.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.520
Right. Good night...

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.740
Looks like everyone’s
having trouble...

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:16.660
Yeah.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.800
Ooh!

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:26.690
Good job, Sarunori!

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.260
So it really is night
all the time here...

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.730
Oh! A shooting star!

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:32.230
Huh?

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.890
Oh, it vanished.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:35.720
Yeah...

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.410
Still, the sky’s really pretty.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.500
There’s so many stars!

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.420
Good evening!

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.520
Oh, good evening!

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.800
It’s actually morning though,
so shouldn’t you say “Good morning”?

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.250
What a headache...

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.170
Were you watching the stars, too?

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:00.710
Yeah, we were.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.130
I was, too!

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.260
My name’s Kirara.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.620
I’m Satoshi.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.280
He’s my partner, Pikachu.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.750
I’m Go.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:12.990
This is my partner, Sarunori.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.650
Hey...

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:22.890
Py!

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.970
Kirara, do you like the stars?

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:33.040
Yeah!
I was looking at them to find Py.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.870
Py turned into a star.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:37.920
Py...?

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.420
Py! Star Shape Pokémon!
Fairy type!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:47.260
Because of its starlike silhouette,
it’s believed to be a star reborn!

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.310
Kirara!

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.390
We should be heading home.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:53.750
Good evening!

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.010
Good morning.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:58.890
I was watching the stars
with those boys.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.230
Oh, thank you.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.990
Mom, can I stay out a little longer?

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.060
Just a little bit longer.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:15.500
She always watches the stars
just like that.

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:17.980
She says
she wants to find Py’s star.

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:19.460
Py’s star?

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:23.890
Py and Kirara were good friends,
and they were always together.

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:26.530
but a couple of days ago,
we finally had to say farewell,

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:29.010
and Py went back to heaven.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:37.520
Kirara was really upset,
so I told her that Py became a star.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:41.770
And then...
She’s been stargazing ever since.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:42.730
I get it.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.650
She must be thinking
about her dear Py.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:50.030
Oh, there was one strange thing...

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.130
It’s something Kirara said.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:58.810
She said she saw a strange Pokémon last week,
and that’s when the endless night started.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.250
Is that true?!

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:04.800
But could a Pokémon really
cause night to last forever?

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.930
It has to be
some sort of coincidence.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.480
Mom! Here I am!

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:13.620
All right. Then let’s go.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.310
Oh, hold on!

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.440
The strange Pokémon you saw,
what did it look like?

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:21.940
Umm...

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:25.380
It was small,
but it had a big eyeball.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.070
It was black,
and shaped like a stick.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:32.080
Now then,
we should get going.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.500
Thank you, you two!

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:35.900
Yeah! Bye bye!

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:36.920
See you!

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.540
What meal is this?

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:43.970
Lunch.

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:46.800
Feels weird eating lunch at night.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.180
What do you think
about that, from before?

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.770
The strange Pokémon?

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:53.850
Yeah.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:56.910
The timing fits far too well
to be a coincidence...

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:59.400
Black, and shaped
like a stick, right?

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.940
I wonder if it’s in an Index...

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:04.740
You found it?

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:07.530
Of course,
right near this town...

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:08.820
I knew it!

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:09.980
Huh?

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.220
We don’t have time to eat.

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:12.460
Thanks for the food!

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:13.870
Let’s go, Satoshi, Pikachu!

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:16.790
Where’re you going, Go?!

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.410
An archaeology museum?

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.630
I have to look into something.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:38.640
What’s wrong, Pikachu?

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:42.390
Pikachu!

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:45.010
Ms. Shirona?

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:46.150
Satoshi!

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.320
It’s been such a long time.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.430
I never expected
to run into you here.

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.280
Have you been well,
too, Pikachu?

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:57.830
Satoshi, I hear you’ve entered
the Pokémon World Championships.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:09:59.760
Yeah!

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:02.670
You’re in the Masters Eight,
right, Ms. Shirona?

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:05.460
I’m gonna make it there
someday, too!

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:08.460
Yes, I’ll eagerly await that.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:11.890
You’re the champion of Sinnoh,
Ms. Shirona, yeah?!

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:13.200
I’m Go!

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:16.380
Satoshi and I are
research fellows at Sakuragi Institute!

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.600
So, what business
brings you here today?

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:22.630
Actually, despite my title,
my forte is archaeology.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:25.340
I study the history
and myths of Pokémon,

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:28.340
and even investigate
rare Pokémon.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:30.610
Really? That’s incredible!

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:35.110
I’m always traveling
around the world to study ruins.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.990
Conducting a study
is what brought me here, too...

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:43.200
We heard it was always night in this town
and came to check it out!

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:49.360
Someone in the town told us a certain Pokémon
might be involved, so we came here to investigate.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:50.780
A certain Pokémon?

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:52.500
You figured it out, Go?

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:56.040
A Pokémon that’s small,
with a big eyeball,

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.260
black, and shaped like a stick!

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.760
It’s Unknown!

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:05.550
Unknown! Symbol Pokémon!
Psychic type!

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:07.760
When alone, nothing happens!

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:11.900
However, if there are two or more,
an odd power emerges!

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:15.280
Unknown are Pokémon
shaped like ancient letters.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:20.460
28 shapes have been found so far,
and they’re a subject of my research, too.

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:25.900
But all we know is that they’re often found near ruins,
and they’re largely a mystery.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:27.630
Unknown, huh...?

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:30.020
Satoshi. Go.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:33.010
Could you tell me the story in full?

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:34.390
Sure!

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.760
I see.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.180
What’s your opinion?

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:43.510
It’s very possible that
a number of Unknown gathered together,

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:47.940
and made that girl’s wish come true
using some unknown power.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.440
So it really was her...!

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:53.770
The Unknown might’ve responded
to her strong emotions.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.700
I’d like to meet and talk to her myself.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.450
Let’s go see her together.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.350
Pocket Monsters!

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:13.590
Kirara!

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.840
Oh, it’s those boys!

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:17.860
Good afternoon!

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:20.090
We meet again,
Pikachu, Sarunori!

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:23.850
Here to watch the stars?

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.200
Yeah!

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.400
May I watch them with you?

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:28.890
You too, miss?

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:31.810
Yeah! I even brought
some doughnuts as a snack.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:34.020
Ta-dah!

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:36.980
They look great!

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:40.060
Have whatever you want.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:42.220
Let’s eat!

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.060
Want half, Pikachu?

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:48.620
I’ll share half with you,
too, Sarunori.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.760
Finished already?
That was fast!

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:56.880
Wow...

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:01.640
Py...

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:07.620
Kirara, do you mind
if I ask you something?

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:08.650
What is it?

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:12.690
The strange Pokémon
you talked about yesterday... Was this it?

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.660
Yeah, that’s it! Li’l Eyeball!

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:19.950
How did you meet?

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:22.700
Well...

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:26.860
Py...

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:36.340
If only I could
watch the stars forever...

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:50.230
Who are you?

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:15.880
Is that so...?

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:19.250
So the Unknown
really were involved...

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:23.350
Kirara, do you know
where the Unknown went after that?

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.560
Li’l Eyeball?

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:25.120
Yeah.

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.340
Why?

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:28.900
It’s never gonna be day again
if things stay like this.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:30.520
Everyone’s having trouble, right?

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:32.980
Trouble?

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:37.860
Yeah. So we’re looking for
a way to fix it.

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:43.400
No!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.860
I wanna keep watching the stars!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:47.740
Kirara?

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.200
I don’t want it to be dawn!

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:51.950
Unknown!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.990
I want it to stay night!

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:05.390
Kirara!

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:07.470
Leave this to us.

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:11.310
Kirara...

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:20.500
Pikachu?!

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:21.770
Watch out.

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.570
That’s an illusion
created by the Unknown.

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:27.010
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:35.590
Follow up with Iron Tail!

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:45.510
You okay, Pikachu?

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:47.680
All right! I’ll help, too!

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.550
Aceburn, go!

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:00.020
An illusion of Aceburn, huh?

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.820
Aceburn, Pyro Ball!

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.490
Follow it up with
Blaze Kick!

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:20.790
No good...
It’s blocking with the same move!

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:23.760
The same moves and equal power.
This could go on forever...

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.260
Leave it to me.

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.400
Gaburias!

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:44.920
Gaburias versus Gaburias?!

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:45.940
Yeah!

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.850
Gaburias! Scale Shot!

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.200
Gaburias! Sandstorm!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.700
Now!

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:13.140
Take to the skies, Gaburias!

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:17.230
She jumped!

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:19.600
She used the sandstorm to hide!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:22.400
Knowing the enemy
would use Sandstorm...

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:23.900
Scale Shot!

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:38.030
That was awesome,
Ms. Shirona!

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:40.300
Thank you, Gaburias.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:42.280
Good work, Aceburn.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:50.210
Kirara!

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:53.820
Py...

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:00.730
I’m glad you’re all right.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:07.860
I was selfish for thinking
night should last forever. I’m sorry.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:10.070
It’s all good.

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:13.260
The stars really are great.

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:17.120
I used to climb up here
and play with Py all the time.

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:21.120
This was Py’s favorite place.

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:23.780
Ms. Shirona...

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:27.090
Why didn’t the Unknown
make an illusion of Py?

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:31.720
Kirara’s greatest wish
must’ve been to see Py again.

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:33.670
Right...

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:41.600
Kirara probably just needed a little more time
to accept parting with Py, I suppose.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:48.020
Py... You became
a shining star.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:53.380
You’ve got lots of friends...
I’m sure you’re really popular up there.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:56.160
So...

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:59.160
I wanted to tell you...

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:04.340
...that I’ll be fine by myself now,
so don’t worry about me.

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:08.590
But...

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:11.670
But I’m so lonely...

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:15.080
I wanna see you...

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:24.880
The Unknown!

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:25.740
Hold on.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.150
Here we go!

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.260
Py...

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:23.410
I’ll be fine, so don’t worry.

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:40.010
Thank you, Py.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.430
Kirara?

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:45.770
Yeah!

00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:48.190
Kirara!

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:53.460
No matter how far apart you are,
you and Py are always gonna be friends!

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:54.930
That’s right!

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:56.070
Yeah!

00:20:56.070 --> 00:21:00.790
You can’t see them in the daylight,
but the stars are always shining.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:05.200
Py’s up there,
even at this very moment.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:06.610
Really?

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.960
Yeah! I get it!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:15.490
Huh? Where’s the Unknown?

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:16.460
They’re gone!

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:18.370
They disappeared, huh?

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:21.220
There’s still much
we don’t know about them.

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:27.220
Li’l Eyeball,
I’ll see you around!

00:21:33.070 --> 00:21:36.010
A mysterious experience
in a little town.

00:21:36.610 --> 00:21:41.760
There’s many more Pokémon shrouded in mystery
all over the world, just waiting to be found.

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:09.680
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:10.950
Go!

00:23:11.860 --> 00:23:14.520
Lucario, time to Mega Evolve!

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:16.670
Hold it!

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:18.860
What about the tools
you need to Mega Evolve?

00:23:18.860 --> 00:23:20.380
That’s what we’re gonna look for!

00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:22.440
Corni’s gonna help out, too!

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:23.760
Let’s try our best, Satoshi!

00:23:24.150 --> 00:23:26.180
Satoshi!

00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:27.860
Go! Lucario!

00:23:28.680 --> 00:23:30.310
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.310 --> 00:23:33.990
Lucarionite!
A Great Adventure on Mega Island!!
